<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<PathAssistant xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        The DIRECT, UNLISTED disposition path, for the Off_Market record type.
        REBUILT 2026-08-19 to the redesigned NINE steps: Disposition Readiness, Broker Selection,
        NDA, Release Materials, Offer Selection, LOI, PSA, Closing, Sale Closes.

        =====================================================================================
        WHAT CHANGED AND WHY, STEP BY STEP.
        =====================================================================================
        REMOVED: the Disposition Offer step (retired value, replaced by Offer Selection) and the
        Completed step (renamed by replacement to Sale Closes).
        ADDED: Broker Selection, Release Materials, Offer Selection, Sale Closes.
        🔴 A BROKER IS NAMED ON THIS PATH TOO. The narrative that "no broker is engaged, so there
        is no BOV Outreach, no Active Listing and no Call for Offers" is retracted in
        Off_Market.recordType-meta.xml. What survives of it is only the narrow truth: there is no
        BOV beauty parade and no public listing, so BOV Outreach and Active Listing remain
        restricted out. The broker is a DIRECT PICK, and the pick is approved.

        ⚠ TWO ORPHAN STEPS WILL RENDER AFTER Sale Closes UNTIL THE PICKLIST CLEANUP WAVE RUNS.
        Disposition Offer and Completed still exist as values and are still listed on the
        Off_Market record type (a record type cannot reference a deleted value, and a metadata
        deploy cannot delete one - Setup can). They have NO step here, so they render with no
        guidance. Deliberate: stale guidance on a stage nothing should reach is worse than none.
        Zero records sit on either value, and there are zero Off_Market rows at all today.

        WHAT EACH STEP'S EXIT IS OWNED BY - and note that TWO of these differ from the on-market
        path, which is the whole reason the two files exist separately:
            Disposition Readiness -> Broker Selection  Sale Decision approval (auto-advance)
            Broker Selection -> NDA                    🔴 Broker Selection APPROVAL, not a button
            NDA -> Release Materials                   MANUAL: Advance to Release Materials
            Release Materials -> Offer Selection       🔴 Select Offer, with NO Active Listing hop
            Offer Selection -> LOI                     Offer Selection approval on the offer
            LOI -> PSA                                 MANUAL: Advance to PSA
            PSA -> Closing                             ContractExecutionService, on PSA execution
            Closing -> Sale Closes                     Closing approval (auto-advance)
        RecordStageAdvanceService's Off_Market map therefore holds only TWO manual hops
        (NDA -> Release Materials and LOI -> PSA) against the on-market four, so the Advance
        button structurally cannot skip the two approval-owned hops above.

        THE CLOSING STEP'S THIRD SENTENCE WAS REWRITTEN, AND IT IS IDENTICAL TO THE ONE ON
        Disposition_Path_On_Market. These two must stay in step with each other - they always
        have. The old sentence told the user to verify the wire FIRST because the AdminOnly
        approval lock would otherwise silently stop Wire_Verification_Rollup. Closing_Approval
        now carries Wire_Verification_Completed__c as an ENTRY CRITERION, so the ordering is
        enforced rather than signposted and the Submit Closing Approval button is hidden until
        the flag is true.

        THE LOI AND PSA STEPS' "arrives in a later change" TEXT IS GONE, BECAUSE IT IS NO LONGER
        TRUE. DispositionStageEntryService auto-creates the sell-side LOI on entry to LOI, and
        Contract_Review__c has a Disposition_PSA record type; both surface in related lists
        already on Disposition_Record_Page.

        🔴 THE ACTIVE-LISTING-CLOCK RETRACTION THAT LIVED IN THIS FILE IS NOT REPEATED HERE. It
        was a note telling the reader not to "fix" the on-market clock text; that text has been
        correct since 2026-08-10 and the full record lives in Disposition_Path_On_Market's own
        comment. Nothing is lost by dropping a pointer to a resolved question, and carrying a
        retraction of a retraction into a rebuilt file would only obscure what actually changed.

        Step ORDER in this file is the design's path order for readability. Runtime display order
        comes from the Disposition_Stage__c picklist value order (sorted = false) filtered by the
        record type, NOT from this file. The master value order was deliberately INTERLEAVED (not
        appended) in the same change so both record types' filtered sequences stay monotonic; the
        arithmetic is in objects/Disposition__c/fields/Disposition_Stage__c.field-meta.xml.

        =====================================================================================
        AMENDED 2026-08-20. THE Broker Selection STEP'S KEY FIELD IS NOW THE LOOKUP.
        =====================================================================================
        fieldNames moved from Selected_Broker__c (Text 255) to Broker__c, the new
        Lookup(Contact) filtered on the Contact.Broker RECORD TYPE. (⚠ CORRECTED 2026-08-20:
        this read "filtered on Is_Broker__c"; the broker definition moved. THE PATH STEP ITSELF
        IS UNAFFECTED — it references Broker__c, the lookup, and never the checkbox, so nothing
        here blocks the checkbox's eventual retirement.) The info text was rewritten in the same change
        because it said "name the broker directly in Selected Broker", which after this change
        is a WRONG INSTRUCTION rather than merely a stale one: the approval gate in
        DispositionApprovalService no longer reads that text field at all, so a user following
        the old sentence would type a name, see it saved, and then be refused at submit with no
        explanation on screen.

        🔴 THE STEP SHOWS THE LOOKUP ONLY. A path step accepts multiple fieldNames, and listing
        Selected_Broker__c alongside it was considered and REJECTED. Off-market that field is now
        DERIVED, stamped from Broker__c in before-context, so displaying it next to its own
        source would sit as a dead interlock on a user's screen and invite a hand edit that
        immediately disagrees with the lookup. This is the same argument both DPEG_Disposition_*
        set headers make for withholding Approval_Advance_Pending__c. Selected_Broker__c is still
        readable on the record page underneath, which is where a read back belongs.

        🔴 Disposition_Path_On_Market IS DELIBERATELY UNCHANGED. Its two Selected_Broker__c
        references stay: on-market the text field is still the real, hand and BOV written value,
        and Broker__c is null and not even rendered on an on-market record. The two paths
        diverge here ON PURPOSE and must not be "made consistent".
        ⚠ CONSEQUENCE FOR A FUTURE RETIREMENT WAVE: an ACTIVE path step referencing a field
        blocks that field's deletion. This change removes the off-market pin on
        Selected_Broker__c, but the on-market path still pins it twice.
    -->
    <active>true</active>
    <entityName>Disposition__c</entityName>
    <fieldName>Disposition_Stage__c</fieldName>
    <masterLabel>Disposition Path Off Market</masterLabel>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <fieldNames>Property_Asset__c</fieldNames>
        <info>Confirm the asset metrics and Argus signal support the sell decision. Use Submit Sale Decision to send it to the principals; approval moves this deal to Broker Selection on its own, so there is no Advance button here.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Disposition Readiness</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <fieldNames>Broker__c</fieldNames>
        <info>No BOV round runs on this path: choose the broker in the Broker field, then use Submit Broker Selection. Only Contacts flagged as brokers can be picked, and Selected Broker fills in automatically from your pick. Approval moves this deal to NDA on its own - there is no Advance button on this step.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Broker Selection</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <fieldNames>NDA_Count__c</fieldNames>
        <fieldNames>Signed_NDA_Count__c</fieldNames>
        <info>Send an NDA to each interested party - one NDA record per party, using the NDAs related list below. Nothing is released until every NDA that was not Declined reads Signed; Advance to Release Materials is refused until then.</info>
        <picklistValueName>NDA</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <fieldNames>Package_Sent__c</fieldNames>
        <info>The NDAs are signed, so the offering materials can go out. Send the package to the cleared parties and log the offers that come back. There is no listing step on this path: use Select Offer once an offer is worth taking to the principals.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Release Materials</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <fieldNames>Accepted_Offer_Price__c</fieldNames>
        <info>Use Select Offer to pick one of the logged offers. Selecting it moves the deal here and sends that offer to the principals in one step. If they reject it the deal stays on this step so another offer can be selected; approval moves it to LOI.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Offer Selection</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <info>The sell-side LOI record is created automatically on entry to this step and appears in the LOIs related list below. Negotiate it there, then use Advance to PSA once terms are agreed.</info>
        <picklistValueName>LOI</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <info>The sell-side contract is tracked on a Contract Review record of the Disposition PSA type, in the Contract Reviews related list below. When it reaches Executed, this deal moves to Closing on its own.</info>
        <picklistValueName>PSA</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <fieldNames>PSA_Executed__c</fieldNames>
        <fieldNames>Title_Company__c</fieldNames>
        <info>PSA Executed = TRUE spawns closing tasks. Wire fraud prevention gate (6 fields) must be complete before wiring. Complete the wire verification first: the Submit Closing Approval button stays hidden until Wire Verification Completed is true, because the approval both requires it and locks this record while it is pending.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Closing</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <fieldNames>Closing_Date__c</fieldNames>
        <fieldNames>Net_Sale_Proceeds__c</fieldNames>
        <info>Deal closed. Confirm the closing date, net sale proceeds, and that the closing statement is on file.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Sale Closes</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <recordTypeName>Off_Market</recordTypeName>
</PathAssistant>
